# app/.env.example -- POINTER FILE, NOT A CONTRACT. Do not add variable names here.
#
# The environment contract is the repository-root `.env.example`. It is normative, it is
# reproduced variable-for-variable in `docs/04-TECH-ARCHITECTURE.md` S11, and it is the
# only file a new variable may be added to. A second list here would be a second source
# of truth, and the two would drift (WP-01 acceptance: "every variable name matches
# `.env.example` exactly").
#
# To run the app locally:
#
#   cd app
#   cp ../.env.example .env      # .env is gitignored at every depth (C7)
#   pnpm install && pnpm db:migrate && pnpm dev
#
# `app/.env` is the file the app actually reads; it is never committed. `app/.env.example`
# is tracked only so the pointer survives a fresh clone.
#
# See: docs/12-OPERATIONS.md S2 (variable-by-variable), S3.6 (install/migrate/seed/run).
